! <solver:p610_t3>
! NAFEMS-style Prandtl strip footing (T3, plane strain, c-phi half-space)
!
! Half-symmetry domain 5 m wide x 5 m deep, footing half-width B/2 = 1 m.
! Mesh: 12 x 10 graded quads -> 240 T3 elements (SW-NE split) (143 nodes).
! BCs: y=-H rigid; x=0 symmetry roller; x=W far-field roller.
! Loading: incremental footing pressure up to 1 * q_ult = 148.3 kPa.
!
! Closed form (Terzaghi-Vesic, gamma = q_surcharge = 0):
!   q_ult = c * Nc                    -> Nc(phi=20) = 14.83
!   With c = 10 kPa, q_ult = 148.3 kPa.
!
! Verification approach (Smith-Griffiths VP solver constraints):
!   p_applied is fixed at the analytical q_ult = c * Nc. The solver must
!   (a) converge in every increment (no iters == limit), and
!   (b) reproduce footing-element syy ~= -q_ult within tolerance %% (load
!       transfer check) while showing plastic flow (s1-s3 ~= 2 c at yield).
!   Identifying the exact collapse load (FE q_ult bracket) requires multi-run
!   load-stepping that is out of scope for the current single-shot solver.
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_elastoplastic
! expected_qult_per_c 14.83
! expected_phi_deg 20
! expected_c_kPa 10
! expected_qult_tolerance_pct 5
! expected_p_applied_kPa 148.3
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
! Mesh size block:
! nels nn np_types
! nels = number of elements
! nn = number of nodes
! np_types = number of material/property types
240  143  1
